From: Macron <macron@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d, opengl32: Write NOOVERWRITE and DISCARD buffer
 uploads without waiting for the GPU.

With buffer maps going through heap memory (0003, 0008), every
DrawPrimitiveUP and every NOOVERWRITE or DISCARD lock of a dynamic
buffer reached the host OpenGL as glBufferSubData into a buffer that
draws already issued still use. Apple's OpenGL on Apple silicon is a
layer over Metal, and there such a glBufferSubData submits the command
buffer and waits for the GPU each time: Ultimate Custom Night spent 77%
of its thread there on an M3, at 5 frames a second.

The heap upload now keeps the map's NOOVERWRITE or DISCARD flag. Such an
upload goes through glBufferWriteUnsynchronizedWINE, which opengl32
hands out from wglGetProcAddress: on the Unix side it maps the range
with GL_MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED_BIT | GL_MAP_INVALIDATE_RANGE_BIT, copies the
data and unmaps, so a 32-bit program never sees a 64-bit pointer. It
returns nothing, so the batching of 0007 queues it like
glBufferSubData. A DISCARD upload first orphans the buffer object with
glBufferData(NULL), so the draws already issued keep the old storage.
Uploads without either flag (UpdateSubResource, initial data) keep
glBufferSubData. WINE_OPENGL_UNSYNCHRONIZED=0 hides the function, and
wined3d falls back to glBufferSubData.

Also fixes a use after free: drawing from a buffer that is still mapped
(wined3d_device_context_flush_mapped_buffer) uploaded the heap copy with
UPLOAD_BO_FREE_ON_UNMAP, so the heap memory was freed while the
application could still write to it and the unmap uploaded it again.
The early upload no longer frees it, and the upload at unmap waits for
the draws that read it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/opengl32/batch.c b/dlls/opengl32/batch.c
index 9d8c7b2..88e8440 100644
--- a/dlls/opengl32/batch.c
+++ b/dlls/opengl32/batch.c
@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@ struct batch
 };
 
 static BOOL batch_disabled;
+static BOOL unsynchronized_writes_disabled;
 static LONG client_arrays; /* a vertex array was set in client memory */
 
 static inline UINT batch_align( SIZE_T size )
@@ -214,12 +215,36 @@ NTSTATUS opengl_unix_call( UINT code, void *args )
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/* Not an OpenGL function: wined3d asks for it with wglGetProcAddress to write
+ * streaming vertex and index data without a GPU wait (unix_wgl.c). It returns
+ * nothing, so it is queued like glBufferSubData. WINE_OPENGL_UNSYNCHRONIZED=0
+ * hides it, and wined3d then uploads with glBufferSubData as before. */
+PROC get_buffer_write_unsynchronized(void)
+{
+    return unsynchronized_writes_disabled ? NULL : (PROC)glBufferWriteUnsynchronizedWINE;
+}
+
+void WINAPI glBufferWriteUnsynchronizedWINE( GLenum target, GLintptr offset, GLsizeiptr size, const void *data )
+{
+    struct buffer_write_unsynchronized_params args = { .teb = NtCurrentTeb(), .target = target, .offset = offset,
+                                                       .size = size, .data = data };
+    NTSTATUS status;
+
+    TRACE( "target %d, offset %Id, size %Id, data %p\n", target, offset, size, data );
+    if ((status = UNIX_CALL( buffer_write_unsynchronized, &args )))
+        WARN( "buffer_write_unsynchronized returned %#lx\n", status );
+    set_context_attribute( -1 /* unsupported */, NULL, 0 );
+}
+
 void batch_process_attach(void)
 {
     char value[8];
 
     if (GetEnvironmentVariableA( "WINE_OPENGL_BATCH", value, sizeof(value) ) && value[0] == '0') batch_disabled = TRUE;
     TRACE( "OpenGL call batching %s\n", batch_disabled ? "disabled" : "enabled" );
+    if (GetEnvironmentVariableA( "WINE_OPENGL_UNSYNCHRONIZED", value, sizeof(value) ) && value[0] == '0')
+        unsynchronized_writes_disabled = TRUE;
+    TRACE( "Unsynchronized buffer writes %s\n", unsynchronized_writes_disabled ? "disabled" : "enabled" );
 }
 
 void batch_thread_detach(void)
